&lt;h2&gt;


  What I Built
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;My best friend &lt;a href="https://github.com/SanjanaG-01" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;@SanjanaG-01&lt;/a&gt; and I are both taking part in Kestra Hacktober this October. Writing the code is not the hard part. Finding an issue nobody has taken yet is.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;On a busy repo, a fresh &lt;code&gt;good first issue&lt;/code&gt; gets its first "can I work on this?" comment within about 20 minutes. By the time you open it, it might already have a pull request, five people asking for it, or a maintainer saying it isn't ready yet. GitHub still shows it as &lt;strong&gt;open&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;So I measured it. GitHub's own search for open, unassigned good first issues in &lt;code&gt;kestra-io/kestra&lt;/code&gt; returned &lt;strong&gt;31 issues&lt;/strong&gt;. When I checked every one of them:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;21&lt;/strong&gt; already had a pull request (one had three)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;8&lt;/strong&gt; had people asking for them in the comments (up to 11 on a single issue)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;2&lt;/strong&gt; were marked "not ready for contributions"&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;0&lt;/strong&gt; were actually free&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;That's why I built &lt;strong&gt;Unclaimed&lt;/strong&gt;. Paste a repository, and it tells you which issues are really &lt;strong&gt;Free&lt;/strong&gt;, which are &lt;strong&gt;Claimed&lt;/strong&gt;, which &lt;strong&gt;Have a PR&lt;/strong&gt;, which are &lt;strong&gt;Assigned&lt;/strong&gt; and which are &lt;strong&gt;Not ready&lt;/strong&gt;, with proof for each one. Instead of opening 30 tabs and reading every comment, my friend sees the free ones first.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F27yyzssri3bmxb5uyn9u.jpg" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F27yyzssri3bmxb5uyn9u.jpg" alt=" " width="799" height="475"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

